--- !u!114 &2106382252
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2106382250}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 2100000, guid: 74df4e230b74f404d9c7e3eb06b78774, type: 2}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 10102, guid: 0000000000000000e000000000000000, type: 0}
    m_FontSize: 19
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 7
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "<b><size=35>Secondary Demo </size></b>\n<b><size=25>First-Person View
    / Non-Player</size></b>\n\nThis demo demonstrates how to use the \"See-through
    Shader\" in the first-person view, where <b>your camera acts as the player</b>
    instead of a dedicated playable character. \nThis effect is achieved by having
    a invisible cube in front of the camera, which takes the role of a player.\n<i>Note:
    Combination of player(third-person) and non-player(first-person)  mode is possible.</i>\n\n<b>How
    to Trigger the STS Effect:</b>\n\tMove the crosshair within a building and the
    See-through Shader will apply the effect on the building.\n\n<b>Scripts Used:</b>\n\tThe
    <b>STSCameraMode.cs</b> script used on the camera for this scene uses NO raycasts
    and determines its logic from calculations. \n\t<i>(Note: Methods 1, 5 and 6
    are definitely the recommended methods using the fpv mode.)</i>\n\n<b>How to
    Change the STS Effect:</b>\n\tTo change the shader settings on the fly go to
    the /core/Resources/STSReferenceMaterials folder and click the\n\trefMaterial
    file.\n\tChange the settings in the refMaterial file and they will be synced
    to the objects.\n\n<b>Controls:</b>\n\t<b>WASD</b>: Move the camera \n\t<b>Hold
    mouse wheel</b>: Freelook \n\t<b>YX</b>: Camera height \n\t<b>QE</b>: Orbit around
    Cube or hold mousewheel and AD.\n     <b>I</b>: Enable / Disable UI.\n\nFor best
    visual experience add the Post Processing Package to your project ( Window >
    Package Manager > Post Processing )\nhttps://www.shadercrew.com\n<b>support@shadercrew.com</b>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
